---
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms · Cadre"
  description="The terms that apply when you use a Cadre service that we host."
>
  <div class="container">
    <Header />
    <main id="main" class="privacy-copy">
      <h1>Terms</h1>
      <p><strong>Last updated: September 19, 2026</strong></p>
      <p>
        These terms apply when you use a Cadre service that we host, including the hosted web app,
        the Cadre mobile app, and cadre.to. They are an agreement between you and Cadre (“we” or
        “us”). If you do not agree to them, do not use the hosted service.
      </p>

      <h2>The software and the service are separate</h2>
      <p>
        The Cadre software is open source under the Apache License, Version 2.0. That licence — not
        these terms — governs what you may do with the source: run it, modify it, and distribute it,
        including commercially, on the conditions the licence states. These terms govern only the
        service we operate for you. If you run Cadre yourself, the operator of that deployment is
        responsible for it, and these terms do not apply to it.
      </p>

      <h2>Your account</h2>
      <p>
        You need an account to use the hosted service. Keep your credentials secure, give us accurate
        information, and tell us promptly if you believe your account has been used without your
        permission. You are responsible for what happens under your account, including what your
        bots do. You must be old enough to enter a contract where you live.
      </p>

      <h2>What bots do on your behalf</h2>
      <p>
        Cadre runs bots that use a browser, a shell, and the tools and accounts you connect. A bot
        acts with the access you give it, so the work it does is attributable to you. Give a bot only
        the access it needs, review the boundaries at which it must ask for approval, and check
        results that matter before relying on them. Models make mistakes, and Cadre does not
        guarantee that a bot's work is correct, complete, or suitable for a purpose.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>You may not use the hosted service to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Break the law, infringe someone's rights, or help someone else do either.</li>
        <li>
          Access an account, system, or dataset you are not authorised to access, or circumvent a
          technical restriction, rate limit, or access control.
        </li>
        <li>
          Send malware, mount a denial-of-service attack, scrape in violation of a site's terms, or
          disrupt the service for other users.
        </li>
        <li>
          Impersonate a person or organisation, or generate content presented as genuine when it is
          not — records, reviews, identity documents, or approvals.
        </li>
        <li>Handle someone else's personal data without a lawful basis to do so.</li>
        <li>Resell or redistribute the hosted service as your own.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We may suspend an account that we reasonably believe is being used this way, or that puts the
        service or other users at risk.
      </p>

      <h2>Your content</h2>
      <p>
        You keep ownership of what you put into Cadre: instructions, messages, files, memories, and
        routines. You give us permission to host, process, and transmit that content only as needed
        to operate the service for you — including sending it to the model providers and connected
        applications you choose. We do not use your content to train models, and we do not sell it.
        You are responsible for having the rights to the content you provide.
      </p>

      <h2>Models and connected services</h2>
      <p>
        Cadre works with model providers and third-party applications you select. What you send to
        one is also governed by that provider's own terms and privacy policy, and its availability,
        pricing, and behaviour are outside our control. Where you supply your own provider keys, the
        cost of that provider's usage is yours.
      </p>

      <h2>Fees</h2>
      <p>
        Where a plan is paid, the price, billing period, and what it includes are stated at the point
        of purchase. Fees are charged in advance and are not refundable except where the law requires
        it. We will give notice before a price change takes effect for you.
      </p>

      <h2>Availability</h2>
      <p>
        We work to keep the hosted service available but do not promise it will be uninterrupted or
        error-free, and we may change or discontinue features. The service is provided as is, without
        warranties of any kind, to the extent the law allows. Nothing here limits a liability that
        cannot be limited by law, including for fraud, or for death or personal injury caused by
        negligence.
      </p>

      <h2>Ending it</h2>
      <p>
        You may stop using the hosted service and delete your account at any time. We may end or
        suspend your access if you materially breach these terms, or if we stop offering the service,
        with reasonable notice where we can give it. You can export your data before you go; after an
        account is deleted, we remove or anonymise it as the privacy policy describes.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms. The date at the top of this page says when they last changed, and
        we will give notice of a material change before it takes effect for you. Continuing to use
        the hosted service after that means the updated terms apply.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact us</h2>
      <p>
        Cadre<br />
        <a href="mailto:hello@cadre.to">hello@cadre.to</a>
      </p>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
